From 06d8e7f07a0d5b9644e5f0e63537b86542aba849 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 23:00:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Plane stress: axial deformation gradient computed by the
 behaviour

In plane stress (PlaneStress and AxisymmetricalGeneralisedPlaneStress),
the axial component of the deformation gradient given by the caller is
no longer used by the interface of the finite strain behaviours: the
conversions of the stresses and of the tangent operators use the one
computed by the behaviour, and the axial component of the strain given
in the Green-Lagrange and Hencky strain frameworks is zero. MGIS and
MTest give an axial component of one. Before:

- behaviours written with F: the computed component was added to the
  given one, the first and second Piola-Kirchhoff stresses being wrong
  by a factor of two;
- Green-Lagrange strain framework: the same addition made the Cauchy
  stress wrong by a factor of two;
- Hencky strain framework: the conversions used the given component,
  the first and second Piola-Kirchhoff stresses being wrong by the axial
  strain, in relative value.

The axial component is described by PlaneStressAxialComponent. With the
displacement gradient, F = I + H on the whole diagonal, as the callers
give F.
